tyle/core/config&quot;</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">import</span> { exclusive } <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;@kirana-style/states/base-ui&quot;</span>\n\n<span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"th-token th-keyword\">default</span> <span class=\"th-token th-function\">defineConfig</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">conditions</span>: { exclusive } })","file":"kirana.config.ts","title":"kirana.config.ts"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The groups are what the library documents: a state and its opposite, both on one\npart."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A state"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"and its opposite"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"checked","source":"checked"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"unchecked","source":"unchecked"}}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"open","source":"open"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"closed","source":"closed"}}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"startingStyle","source":"startingStyle"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"endingStyle","source":"endingStyle"}}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"valid","source":"valid"}}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"invalid","source":"invalid"}}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Ark UI and React Aria mark those with one attribute's values or not at all, so\ntheir lists are empty."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"one-look-for-several-libraries","children":[{"type":"text","value":"One look for several libraries"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A design system that writes each component once for several libraries spreads\nevery library's key for a state: Base UI's "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-string\">[data-starting-style]</span>","source":"[data-starting-style]"}},{"type":"text","value":" and React Aria's\n"},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-string\">[data-entering]</span>","source":"[data-entering]"}},{"type":"text","value":" for a popup's first frame. A component is built on one library,\nso those keys never meet on an element, but nothing in the selectors says so, and\neach pair is reported. "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">exclusiveAcross</span>()","source":"exclusiveAcross()"}},{"type":"text","value":" gives the compiler one vocabulary per\nlibrary; two keys that no single library sets are then exclusive:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code","tagName":"md-code","attributes":{},"c